    "body": "I have two problems with this PR:\r\n\r\n1. It claims to fix an issue, but I don't think it fixes it since the issue is also about the \"Writing HTML\" section.\r\n\r\n2. I think this change ends up being confusing since the normative prose doesn't say anything about the content model. It's only the example that mentions it. So at best we could say something \"see example for clarification\". \"See prose\" indicates to me there's some kind of normative definition (as is the case elsewhere).",
